OL,3,GNEWSAHow you can celebrate Diwali for
OL,4,Afree across the West Midlands
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs thousands of people across the West
OL,7,FMidlands prepare to celebrate Diwali, a
OL,8,Fseries of free light switch-ons,
OL,9,Fcultural events and firework displays
OL,10,Fwill be held across the region,
OL,11,Fbringing communities together to mark
OL,12,Fthe occasion.
OL,14,FKnown as the Festival of Lights, Diwali
OL,15,Ffalls on 8 November this year and is
OL,16,Fcelebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains,
OL,17,Fas well as some Buddhists around the
OL,18,Fworld.
